<title>UK: UK clears Vodafone, Campbell, Inchcape deals.</title>
<headline>UK clears Vodafone, Campbell, Inchcape deals.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Secretary of State for Trade and Industry Ian Lang said on Thursday he had decided not to refer the following mergers to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission.</p>
<p>--Vodafone Plc's proposed acquisition of The People's Phone Company Plc.</p>
<p>--Kingspan Group Plc's proposed acquisition of Ward Building Systems Ltd.</p>
<p>--Rugby Group Plc's acquisition of Boral UK Limited's Pozzolanic Lytag Ltd and Lytag Ltd.</p>
<p>--Campbell Soup Company's proposed acquisition of Grand Metropolitan Plc's Erasco Group.</p>
<p>--Intertek Testing Services Ltd's acquisition of Inchcape Plc's Inchcape Testing Services Ltd.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
